# "The video card's interrupts" — a handler on port B counts the end of every
# picture for one second of SysDelay. Sixty a second, near enough.

console video
cycles 3000000

screen ^COUNTING PICTURES FOR ONE SECOND\s*$
# 60 or 61: the second starts wherever the card happens to be in a picture
# when RUN lands, and the machine runs free between the harness's commands,
# so which of the two a run sees depends on the host (CI has seen 61).
screen ^6[01] PICTURES\s*$
